NASA Anomaly detection - Dockerized ML Project

Overview
This project implements anomaly detection on NASA turbofan engine degradation simulation data using Isolation Forest algorithm. This algorithm was chosen as it is good for high dimenional data without the assumption of normal distribution and is unsupervised The pipeline is containerized with Docker.

The model is trained with data and the plots to show anomalies prediction results on test and train data written into CSV output files are saved inside the container. 

Project Structure
CMAPSS_ML/
|----CMAPSS_IsolationForest.py
|----DataReadme.txt
|----Dockerfile 
|----README
|----requirements.txt
|----test_FD001.txt
|----train_FD001.txt
|----ouptut/
    |----TestAnomalyResults
    |----TrainAnomalyResults
    |----plot/

* Dockerfile
    Defines the container environment using python:3.9-slim as the base image.
        The Dockerfile has comments included for every execution

* requirements.txt list all dependencies in PyPI version only

* train_FD001.txt   
    Holds the training data

* test_FD001.txt
    Hold the test data

* DataReadme
    Information on training and test data

*ouptut
    *TestAnomalyResults
        Anomalies predicted in test data
    *TrainAnomalyResults
        Anomalies predicted in train data
    *plots/
        Plots with anomalies and correct data points

* CMAPSS_IsolationForest.py
    ML script to train the model and classify the data points


PROJECT WORKFLOW
* Needs the folder 
    CMAPSS_ML/
        |----CMAPSS_IsolationForest.py
        |----DataReadme.txt
        |----Dockerfile 
        |----README
        |----requirements.txt
        |----test_FD001.txt
        |----train_FD001.txt

* Prepare environment
    WSL environment enabled
    Docker is installed and running

*Steps to follow
    1. Copy folder to own system
    2. Open terminal in teh project folder
    3. Build Docker image
        * Docker Image Build
            cd ~/DockerPractice/CMAPSS_ML
            docker build -t nasa-anomaly . # Docker reads the Dockerfile. Creates working directory inside the container, copies the requirements first, installs the dependencies and then copies rest of the files from host to container. Sequence written in the Dockerfile
            mkdir output
            docker run -rm -v $(pwd)/output: /app/output nasa-anomaly  #--rm Removes container after exit
                #-v use volume mounts to get outputs on host 
                # $(pwd)/output:/app/output  maps host folder to container folder
            docker ps -a # verify container execution

WORKFLOW

    Host Folder (~/DockerPractice/CMAPSS_ML)
|---- train/
|----test/
|---- CMAPSS_IsolationForest.py
|---- output/  <-- mapped to container

         │  docker build
         ▼

Container /app
|---- train/   (copied from host)
|---- test/    (copied from host)
|---- CMAPSS_IsolationForest.py
|---- output/  <-- writes CSV here

         │  docker run with volume
         ▼

Host Folder ~/DockerPractice/CMAPSS_ML/output/
|---- TrainAnomalyResults.csv
|---- TestAnomalyResults.csv

    
